WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:06.100
Speaker 1: there is a reason why in this story's
YouTube clip.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:13.090
I'm using the word accidentally in quotes,
because when it comes to accidentally firing

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:17.090
a gun, we really shouldn't be using the word
accidental.

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:19.160
We should be using the word negligent.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.350
We should be using the word reckless.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:27.460
The headline, as it's being reported by W.L.
Wex and others, is that a woman had a gun

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.330
in her purse during a basketball game.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:34.410
OK, and she accidentally fired the gun.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:38.350
I don't think accidentally is really the right
word that we should be using here, but the

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:45.540
story is a woman has been given a $500 bond
after firing a gun at a basketball game in

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:49.840
Madison, Madison, Mississippi, that is according
to police.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.879
The incident happened inside the gym at Rosa
Scott School Monday night during the game.

00:00:54.879 --> 00:01:01.039
Khashan Alexis McReynolds reached into her
purse to grab her phone but accidentally fired

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:02.039
her gun.

00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:07.700
Nobody was hurt, but the game was suspended
while investigators escorted Mike Runnels

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.759
to a secure office inside the school.

00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:16.329
McReynolds did have an enhanced concealed
carry permit or permit, some folks like to

00:01:16.329 --> 00:01:19.909
say, which allowed her to have the firearm
at the event.

00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:24.399
However, she was charged with discharging
a firearm within the city limits of Madison

00:01:24.399 --> 00:01:27.159
in violation of the City of Madison ordinance.

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:36.409
Mick Runnels was given a $500 bond and a court
date to appear before Madison Municipal Court.

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:39.790
Accidentally means negligent discharge.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:45.799
We have to stop normalizing these incidents
by calling them accidents, and that's why

00:01:45.799 --> 00:01:49.829
I'm calling this quote accidentally.

00:01:49.829 --> 00:01:51.299
It's the wrong word.

00:01:51.299 --> 00:01:59.189
It was a negligent discharge that was related
to the reckless handling of a firearm.

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:03.459
Imagine now it didn't happen here, but it
happens all the time.

00:02:03.459 --> 00:02:08.649
Imagine ending someone's life with such a
dumb mistake.

00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:09.739
It's happened.

00:02:09.739 --> 00:02:11.569
We've covered the stories even.

00:02:11.569 --> 00:02:17.320
I mean, this is now kind of a whole other
topic in a sense, because some people are

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:23.710
pointing out this was a legal concealed carry
individual license.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:28.159
Even the classes that are run in many states
are kind of a joke.

00:02:28.159 --> 00:02:31.110
As I've said before, I don't talk about whether
I own guns.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.640
So I'm just going to couch this generally.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:34.650
There are many liberals.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:40.950
I know that own guns who have said the classes
really can be passed by morons.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:46.540
And we know that to be true because of the
number of instances where it's not a crime.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:51.659
Someone who criminally obtained a gun doesn't
have a permit, doesn't have a concealed carry

00:02:51.659 --> 00:02:52.860
permit, whatever.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:58.219
People who are licensed and up to date on
everything that they're supposed to do, who

00:02:58.219 --> 00:03:02.400
behave recklessly and negligently with firearms.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:07.780
And if and until and I'm like a broken record
on this, if an until accidents are actually

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:11.200
treated like the serious negligence that they
are.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.540
I don't think we're going to see anything
change.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:18.580
The Madison Cawthorn incident is just a perfect
example of this, where Republican Congressman

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.650
Madison Cawthorn tried to board a plane from.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:23.640
I think it was somewhere to Charlotte.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.969
Maybe it was Asheville to Charlotte or something
like that.

00:03:26.969 --> 00:03:32.680
And he tried in the sense that he had a firearm
in his carry on.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:36.579
He tried to board a plane to get through TSA
security with a firearm, and it was shocked

00:03:36.579 --> 00:03:37.579
to, oh, it was an accident.

00:03:37.579 --> 00:03:40.030
He didn't know the gun was in the bag, as
if that's an excuse.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:45.739
If you don't know where your firearm is, if
you believe the firearm that you're responsible

00:03:45.739 --> 00:03:49.930
for, which is a huge responsibility if you
believe that firearm is in one place and it's

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.969
actually in a different place, that's reckless.

00:03:52.969 --> 00:03:53.969
That's negligent.

00:03:53.969 --> 00:03:58.579
It's not an excuse to say I didn't think it
was in my in my bag.

00:03:58.579 --> 00:04:01.689
That's an indication that we should be reviewing
whether you should even be allowed to have

00:04:01.689 --> 00:04:02.689
that gun at all.

00:04:02.689 --> 00:04:06.859
So we're going to, you know, it's an issue
we're going to continue covering and the extent

00:04:06.859 --> 00:04:09.680
to which this is something Democrats should
should be running on.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:14.700
I've said before, I don't know that it's pragmatically
speaking a good issue to win elections, particularly

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:19.459
in places where it's very purple, purple to
reddish, but it's an issue that's not going

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:19.959
away anytime soon.

